  "source": "one-continuous-master",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "While Geppetto sat in prison, Pinocchio celebrated being completely free.",
      "start": 0.036,
      "end": 5.413
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "The century-old Talking Cricket warned him to respect his father.",
      "start": 5.413,
      "end": 11.204
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "Pinocchio rejected school, honest work, and every uncomfortable piece of advice.",
      "start": 11.204,
      "end": 17.473
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "When the Cricket predicted trouble, the angry puppet threw a hammer.",
      "start": 17.473,
      "end": 22.619
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "His victory felt empty as hunger filled the cold, bare house.",
      "start": 22.619,
      "end": 27.395
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "The only egg cracked open, and a cheerful chick escaped through the window.",
      "start": 27.395,
      "end": 33.675
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "Outside, Pinocchio begged for food but received a bucket of cold water.",
      "start": 33.675,
      "end": 39.291
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "He returned soaked and fell asleep with his feet beside the stove.",
      "start": 39.291,
      "end": 44.765
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "By morning, both wooden feet had burned completely away.",
      "start": 44.765,
      "end": 49.545
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "Geppetto returned from prison and listened to Pinocchio's desperate story.",
      "start": 49.545,
      "end": 55.291
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "Though he was hungry too, the old man offered his last three pears.",
      "start": 55.291,
      "end": 61.33
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "Pinocchio first refused the skins and cores, then ate them gratefully.",
      "start": 61.33,
      "end": 67.256
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "Geppetto agreed to replace the feet only after a sincere promise.",
      "start": 67.256,
      "end": 72.295
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "The puppet apologized and declared that he would go to school.",
      "start": 72.295,
      "end": 77.127
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "His father carved and attached two sturdy new wooden feet.",
      "start": 77.127,
      "end": 82.475
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "Finally, Geppetto sold his only coat to buy the promised primer.",
      "start": 82.475,
      "end": 87.52
    }
  ],
